WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:43.960
Few birds have caught the human imagination as powerfully as the eagle. Throughout the

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:50.280
centuries this majestic bird of prey has been the symbol of strength and courage. That is

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:57.440
the perfection of its design. There are 60 different kinds of eagles throughout the world

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:05.520
and all have this basic body plan. But eagles hunt many different kinds of prey and to succeed

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:20.880
they've had to adapt the classic eagle blueprint and these modifications have been spectacular.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:40.520
This is the signature of the world's most successful eagle. In terms of design the golden

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:46.440
eagle is a classic model. With just a few modifications it has colonized much of the

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:55.640
world. The trademark of all eagles is a hooked rapier like bill but they use other tools

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:02.720
for killing. The back talon pierces like a bayonet. The rest act like grappling arms

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:10.720
crushing prey with an incredible force. Its surveillance gear is equally powerful magnifying

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:17.180
two and a half times and resolving eight times more detail than the human eye. It can see

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:32.720
prey a mile and a half away. Flight reveals another defining feature. Broad wings that

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:47.920
float on air. In the slightest updraft five kilos of bird becomes as light as a feather.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.920
Through evolution prey has become the natural designer refining each eagle's body plan

00:02:53.920 --> 00:03:19.640
and behavior. In Alaska a cauldron of early morning mist shrouds another classic model.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:28.800
One specifically for fishing. The icy advance of the Arctic winter has driven golden eagles

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.800
further south. But for the bald eagle the chill cat river provides a welcome staging

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:59.240
post on their migration. The black and white livery is the trademark of many fish eagles.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:04.680
The steamy backdrop has formed as thermal springs percolate the river like a natural

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:15.160
jacuzzi. Up to three thousand bald eagles gather here enticed by the fishy banquet hidden

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:26.600
beneath the icy surface. Volcanic heat acts as an icebreaker allowing salmon to spawn

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:40.000
during the cold heart of winter. These are chum salmon. Having spawned their next generation

00:04:40.000 --> 00:05:03.880
they're waiting to die. Like vultures the bald eagles simply have to bide their time.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:13.560
Pickings are easy but the competition is fierce. He proclaims possession but still needs to

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:39.040
feed quickly. Fights are highly ritualized. Pride the only injury.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:54.640
A high concentration of food allows many eagles to coexist. A fine balance between tolerance

00:05:54.640 --> 00:06:06.440
and aggression results in ritualized combat. They might slip and slide but grip pads on

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:21.360
their talons will clamp the slipperiest fish. Their two-toned uniform means that birds with

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:41.720
food become flying advertisements easily seen by other birds. But bald eagle etiquette allows

00:06:41.720 --> 00:07:09.000
the bird in possession a moment to feed before the raider attacks.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.200
It might look like a bun fight but among the scrum the birds are taking turns. Ultimately

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:32.000
they all have a seat at the table. All fish eagles share similar characteristics and most

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:39.340
are gregarious. In contrast other eagles tend to be solitary. Among them are the powerful

00:07:39.340 --> 00:08:03.000
forest eagles of the tropics. A long tail and short wings is their unique brand mark.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:15.640
The crown is Africa's most ferocious eagle. Its crested headgear only adds to its imposing

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:22.360
appearance. It hardly needs such embellishment. The nature of its prey says everything about

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:42.200
its power. In response the eagle has developed awesome weapons.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:09:08.520
The crown is marvelously adapted for forest hunting. The long tail gives maneuverability

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:31.560
while short wings squeeze it through the smallest gap.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:37.600
Forest eagles have a body plan shaped for hunting in woodland. Golden eagles could not

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:42.560
survive here although by changing their behavior they have invaded some surprisingly wooded

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:56.000
places. In the Dardia mountains in Greece golden eagles hunt over open forest but their

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:08.320
long wings create problems when chasing their prey among the trees. They have found an unlikely

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:22.120
alternative prey. Soaring as a search technique is equally effective for finding tortoises.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:27.480
But stooping seems like overkill and to avoid crashing into trees it applies the brakes

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:38.280
as it nears the ground. The armored shell presents an intriguing challenge. It simply doesn't

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:56.320
have the right tools for the job. Its solution is ingenious. It flies to a favored site where

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:18.960
a rocky outcrop acts like a natural anvil. It then gains height.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:46.800
It then safely parachutes into the clearing. The impact separates the tortoise shell into

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:58.560
two halves like loosening a lid. Eagles here feed almost exclusively on tortoises and they

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:09.280
have all learned the same trick. In forests tree nests are common but too many trees and

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:27.160
the eagles can't hunt even for tortoises. Dense forest has acted as a barrier preventing

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:35.200
the golden eagle reaching South America and Southeast Asia. But it nests throughout Europe,

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:43.840
North America and Asia making it the most widespread and successful of eagles. Strangely

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:53.680
the golden doesn't nest in Africa. The reason why involves other eagles. These are step

00:12:53.680 --> 00:13:00.340
and lesser spotted eagles riding a thermal on their way to Africa. Using broad wings

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:12.400
for lift they glide from this invisible elevator in search of another. They are now over Israel.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:23.360
By gliding from thermal to thermal they will save energy on the long journey ahead. Using

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:39.160
this energy-saving flight they may travel as much as 4,000 miles without stopping for

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:53.760
a few minutes. They undertake this marathon flight because in their home on the steppes

00:13:53.760 --> 00:14:01.400
of Asia their mammal prey hibernates over winter. Step eagles are smaller relatives

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:08.960
of the golden eagle but only they migrate. By the time one reaches Africa it's lost a

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:34.480
third of its body weight. In their northern homes they feed on small mammals but here

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:52.040
their tastes change. There are 16 other eagle species in Africa so to avoid competition

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:58.280
the steppe needs to find a gap in the food market. Besides scavenging it eats mainly

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:08.880
termites. Its African cousin the tawny prefers small mammals so the two avoid conflict by

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:21.720
pursuing different prey. Another way of winning the endless competition for food is to be

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:43.160
the biggest. The marshal weighs in at 6 kilos with a wingspan of over 2 metres. This huge

00:15:43.160 --> 00:16:07.160
and ferocious bird can show surprising tenderness. Just a single chick is reared every two years,

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:12.640
family planning that matches the number of birds to the available space. Amazingly each

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:21.360
pair of marshals needs a hundred square miles to itself. Big birds not only need a lot of

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:47.000
space they also hunt big prey. Even small antelope like this daika are tackled.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:17:09.640
The

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:33.400
hunter exploits cover as far as possible. Surprise is everything. Even an eagle as powerful

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:44.960
as a marshal only succeeds one time in five. The battler has a bizarre and unique shape

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:52.600
that helps it find a meal. It intersperses its ungainly flaps with short glides trying

00:17:52.600 --> 00:18:13.000
to gain height. Its tail is too short to serve as an effective stabiliser. But soaring reveals

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:19.160
the effectiveness of its body pan. Its comparative instability responds instantly to the tiniest

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:29.040
updrafts. The short tail makes tiny quick adjustments allowing it to soar at low altitude

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:38.600
as it looks for carrion. With scarcely a wing beat it can search 200 miles in a day. As

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:54.640
it lands its aerial grace vanishes again. Its flight technique allows it to survey huge

00:18:54.640 --> 00:19:11.640
areas and spot carcasses that other eagles miss. With such a diversity of eagles in Africa

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:38.280
it seems surprising that the golden isn't among them. But perhaps it is. Soaring above

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:44.080
the rock copies of the motopos in Zimbabwe is the answer to the mystery of the missing

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:52.640
eagle. These are black eagles. Except for the colour of their plumage they're almost

00:19:52.640 --> 00:20:04.160
identical in form to the golden. To survive here the archetypal generalist, the golden

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:18.040
eagle has had to become a specialist. Remarkably it now hunts just a single prey, a distant

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:27.440
relative of the elephant. Rock hyrax may look like rodents but their hooves hint at this

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:50.560
closer and more surprising relationship. The landscape of broken rocks offers their prey

00:20:50.560 --> 00:21:09.640
a maze of escape routes. To increase the element of surprise eagles often collaborate in pairs.

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:22.040
They add to their prey's confusion by hunting with the sun behind them. But the hyrax has

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:47.440
evolved a countermeasure, an iris in its eye that cuts down the glare. Being detected

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:53.000
might seem to be the ruin of a hunt but this eagle is a decoy, attracting attention away

00:21:53.000 --> 00:22:22.960
from its team mate. For black eagles competition starts with hatching. This chick is a rare

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:34.840
species. It's three days younger and here sibling rivalry can lead to murder. The parents

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:49.980
are attentive, bringing back garlands of aromatic leaves to use as fly repellents. The black

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:56.940
eagle uses this natural insecticide to fumigate the nest as many eagles do but her devotion

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:09.540
will not help the new hatchling. The older chick has summarily dealt with the competition.

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:22.640
This may seem harsh but it has good reason. In the tropics there are few vacant territories.

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:42.440
Even one extra eagle may have trouble finding a space. In temperate zones populations turn

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:48.520
over quickly so there eagles spread the risk by rearing more. But here one offspring is

00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:58.520
the more prudent investment. Laying two eggs is an insurance policy just in case one for

00:23:58.520 --> 00:24:11.520
some reason is lost. With so much competition in Africa any new environment is soon fully

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:27.840
colonized. These are the skeletons of trees drowned when Zimbabwe's Kariba dam was created

00:24:27.840 --> 00:24:45.280
in the 1950s. They now provide perches and nest sites for the African fish eagle. This

00:24:45.280 --> 00:24:51.120
species shares many characteristics with the American bald eagle. They both have a bill

00:24:51.120 --> 00:25:01.120
perfect for filleting and talons that act as fish spears. They also have grip pads on

00:25:01.120 --> 00:25:11.520
their talons and long slender legs that snatch their prey from the water. Because of internal

00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:19.680
reflections the fish can only see out of the water through a narrow window directly above.

00:25:19.680 --> 00:25:31.600
The fish eagle exploits the fish's blind spot when hunting. It swoops in low and takes the

00:09:07.540 --> 00:26:12.640
day hunting. Despite the occasional slip up they're so efficient that they can

00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:39.840
sometimes spend as little as eight minutes a day hunting. There is only one type of fish

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:56.000
eagle in Africa so it has no direct rivals. It's found wherever there is water.

00:26:56.000 --> 00:27:07.280
But not all water contains fish. This is Bogoria, a soda lake in Kenya. No fish live in this

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:34.080
caustic water. But eagles still hunt here. Their prey are flamingos.

00:27:34.080 --> 00:27:55.360
The fish eagle is spoilt for choice. Up to two million flamingos may congregate here.

00:27:55.360 --> 00:28:00.000
Several pairs of eagles live on the lake but they never seem to breed here. Perhaps the

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:17.040
flamingos are simply too heavy to carry to the nest. As the flamingos filter algae from

00:28:17.040 --> 00:28:33.520
the caustic water they always keep a watchful eye on the sky.

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:58.000
The eagle seeks out weak or isolated birds.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:14.480
Its technique is to prevent the prey getting fully airborne.

00:29:14.480 --> 00:29:42.960
Dive bombing weakens the bird.

00:29:42.960 --> 00:30:01.680
The fish eagle may have adapted to new food but so have other eagles. The scavenging step

00:30:01.680 --> 00:30:16.560
eagles that first took us to Africa have here become pirates. For the fish eagle it's easier

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:36.240
to hunt again. It leaves the fighting to others.

00:30:36.240 --> 00:30:54.320
It's not only eagles that are its competitors. Black kites mob fish eagles relentlessly.

00:30:54.320 --> 00:31:20.600
Talons can be formidable defensive weapons but contact is rare. Such aerial manoeuvring

00:31:20.600 --> 00:31:32.120
has developed into highly ritualised displays among some fish eagles. The white bellied

00:31:32.120 --> 00:31:41.240
fish eagle lives along the coasts of South East Asia. But here near Penang competition

00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:58.680
comes from a surprising and dramatic source. This aerial battle is for territory. An eagle

00:31:58.680 --> 00:32:21.080
may rest from the fray but by simply watching the dog fight it risks losing airspace.

00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:33.200
These fights demand precision flying and often climax with the presenting of talons. As the

00:32:33.200 --> 00:32:52.480
eagles push their stunt flying to the limit they make contact. Talons lock and the eagles

00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:57.840
spiral.

00:32:57.840 --> 00:33:03.440
These spectacular contests are highly ritualised and talon grappling has become one of the

00:33:03.440 --> 00:33:19.600
most astonishing displays of aerobatics in the natural world. Cart wheeling is a game

00:33:19.600 --> 00:33:32.440
of dare that can end in death. The ultimate test of nerve. Other eagles cart wheel but

00:33:32.440 --> 00:33:50.640
fish eagles are the stars. Forced to fight over the same food they have become skilled

00:33:50.640 --> 00:33:55.800
in the art. This is not an eel. It is one of the most venomous snakes on earth. It needs

00:33:55.800 --> 00:34:07.880
to be handled with care.

00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:13.240
Sea snakes congregate here to breed and the eagle has refined its hunting skills to such

00:34:13.240 --> 00:34:27.120
a degree that it can grapple with this potentially lethal prey. The eagle has no immunity to

00:34:27.120 --> 00:34:40.440
the venom so it is forced into a deadly juggling act. Power diving ensures that the snakes

00:34:40.440 --> 00:34:58.680
are taken by surprise.

00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:04.120
Fishing over the open sea has led to its wings becoming long and narrow a shape more common

00:35:04.120 --> 00:35:18.840
among sea birds. This fish eagle has been able to adapt its fishing technique to a different

00:35:18.840 --> 00:35:40.840
prey but the forest contains eagles that make hunting snakes a speciality. The crested serpent

00:35:40.840 --> 00:35:51.720
eagle belongs to a group known as the snake eagles. Such a specialist prey needs a radical

00:35:51.720 --> 00:36:11.480
reshape of the eagle. It is adapted for walking and climbing allowing it to search in dense

00:36:11.480 --> 00:36:20.800
woodland. To tackle potentially venomous prey it pays to take it by surprise. Its small

00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:41.080
size and relatively short wings allow it to fly amongst dense foliage. This serpent eagle

00:36:41.080 --> 00:36:54.720
has adapted to forest life. It is a home that it shares with another group of eagles. Short

00:36:54.720 --> 00:37:00.120
wings for saving space and a long tail for maneuverability is the recurrent solution

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:13.880
for the life in the forest. It is a blueprint that has been perfected by the hawk eagles.

00:37:13.880 --> 00:37:19.800
This is Blythe's hawk eagle. Its conspicuous crest is found in most forest birds and is

00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:25.440
probably a signaling device. Long claws on the talons are for plucking birds from the

00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:34.960
air for this eagle is a fast and dynamic hunter. It is also tiny. It is among the smallest

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:42.160
eagles being no bigger than a pigeon. Being small has advantages in the forest. In other

00:37:42.160 --> 00:37:49.280
environments eagles have found advantages at the opposite end of the scale. Japanese

00:37:49.280 --> 00:38:00.920
fishing boats off Hokkaido are a magnet to the world's biggest fish eagle. With a two

00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:07.200
and a half meter wingspan and weighing in at an incredible nine kilos these stellas

00:38:07.200 --> 00:38:18.560
are the sumo wrestlers of the eagle world. Closely related to the bald eagle but twice

00:38:18.560 --> 00:38:29.600
the size they have a bill larger than any other bird of prey. The fishing fleet provides

00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:40.480
easy pickings. The fish that fall from the nets. Even large fish are just a sushi snack

00:38:40.480 --> 00:38:58.440
for these huge eagles. Stellas are among our rarest eagles but as much as a third of the

00:38:58.440 --> 00:39:21.040
world's population may gather here drawn by free seafood. Remarkably in strong winds

00:39:21.040 --> 00:39:25.640
even the world's heavyweights sometimes have problems losing height. They may have to spill

00:39:25.640 --> 00:39:51.280
the air from their wings by whistling. As they squabble over these free handouts the

00:39:51.280 --> 00:40:05.240
heaviest and largest of the fish eagles profits from human activity. In the Philippines the

00:40:05.240 --> 00:40:16.100
greatest of the forest eagles is not faring so well. This is the mighty Philippine eagle

00:40:16.100 --> 00:40:28.840
surely the most impressive of all the family. Its headdress is a flamboyant crown that outclasses

00:40:28.840 --> 00:40:36.360
any other eagle. At over a meter in height this is the world's tallest eagle. Its splendid

00:40:36.360 --> 00:40:45.400
crown only enhances its record breaking size. Like the crowned eagle of Africa its talons

00:40:45.400 --> 00:41:03.320
are for monkey sized prey. In the air it is no less impressive. Its wings are very broad

00:41:03.320 --> 00:41:21.480
and have a surface area larger than any other eagle. This shape is suited to slow flight

00:41:21.480 --> 00:41:36.200
and maneuverability in the forest. But this eagle holds a less enviable record that of

00:41:36.200 --> 00:42:00.360
rarity. This is the first film taken at the nest in the last 20 years. Philippine eagles

00:42:00.360 --> 00:42:06.360
rear just one chick. This one is three months old. It will be another six months before

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:16.160
it's fledged and the parents will not breed for another two years. Such a low turnover

00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:22.480
suited a world before human intervention. The eagle is now unable to reproduce quickly

00:42:22.480 --> 00:42:31.000
enough. This remarkable view of the world's most endangered eagle removing a monkey's

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:47.560
tail is now sadly a rare sight. The Philippine eagle's forest home is rapidly disappearing.

00:42:47.560 --> 00:43:16.920
As the rainforest vanishes so too do the eagles. Fewer than 200 may now remain in the wild.

00:43:16.920 --> 00:43:39.080
The fate of this magnificent forest eagle now rests in human hands. Among the world's

00:43:39.080 --> 00:43:46.840
largest eagles, the golden eagle group has its own star. The distinctive tail of this

00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:53.560
huge eagle has given the species its name. The wedge tail is derived from the golden

00:43:53.560 --> 00:43:59.200
eagle. When it arrived in Australia, it found a continent empty of other eagles. Without

00:43:59.200 --> 00:44:09.520
competition it evolved unchecked. Even young kangaroos aren't safe from this fearsome

00:44:09.520 --> 00:44:25.880
hunter. It's found throughout the outback and is Australia's only large bird of prey.

00:44:25.880 --> 00:44:30.520
Its population exploded when forests were cleared for grazing and it thrived on the

00:44:30.520 --> 00:44:43.360
introduced rabbits. Now an introduced virus is wiping out its new rabbit prey so it's

00:44:43.360 --> 00:44:53.980
turning back to the old. Such young kangaroos present a challenge but its lance-like talents

00:44:53.980 --> 00:45:11.040
have been known to pierce a lung and even kill adults. In the hunt, the fan-like tail

00:45:11.040 --> 00:45:38.800
gives quick maneuvering. But even the fast turns that such a shape allows can be out-maneuvered.

00:45:38.800 --> 00:45:59.800
Eating traditional prey is difficult but today there are more modern ways of getting meals.

00:45:59.800 --> 00:46:05.720
Roadside eating is the labor-saving alternative. There are no vultures in Australia and the

00:46:05.720 --> 00:46:15.040
wedge tail has taken on their role too. The wedge tail is a golden eagle whose habits

00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:30.440
have diversified in the absence of competition. But even the archetypal golden eagle can show

00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:40.320
similar versatility. This is Kamchatka, a remote wasteland in eastern Siberia. Golden

00:46:40.320 --> 00:46:46.440
eagles are only able to survive here because of the presence of stellar eagles. Here the

00:46:46.440 --> 00:46:53.520
stellars fish for spawning salmon as the bald eagles did in Alaska. Only stellars have bills

00:46:53.520 --> 00:47:02.360
strong enough to break through the sockeyes armored skin. But the golden eagle shows

00:47:02.360 --> 00:47:15.320
the adaptability of its superb body plan by becoming a scavenger. It needs to feed quickly

00:47:15.320 --> 00:47:22.200
but by taking its chances it can survive in one of the most inhospitable places on earth.

00:47:22.200 --> 00:47:39.160
No other eagle is so successful. It's a living testimony to the perfection of a classic design.

00:47:39.160 --> 00:47:55.400
More than any other, this flying masterpiece lays claim to a simple accolade, the word

00:47:55.400 --> 00:48:08.080
children.

00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:27.460
you
